<article class="env-variant" id="05VF">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05VF">Variant <span data-tag="05VF">7.7.4.8</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}$ denote the $\infty $-category of (small) $\infty $-categories (Construction <a data-tag="0209" href="/tag/0209">5.5.3.1</a>). The $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}$ has disjoint coproducts: if $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_0$ and $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_1$ are small $\infty $-categories, then the disjoint union $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}= \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_0 \amalg \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_1$ is a coproduct of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_0$ with $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_1$ in the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}$ (Example <a data-tag="03EP" href="/tag/03EP">7.6.1.20</a>). The inclusion functors $\iota _0: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_0 \hookrightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ and $\iota _1: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_1 \hookrightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ are fully faithful, and are therefore monomorphisms in the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}$ (Corollary <a data-tag="04W6" href="/tag/04W6">5.5.3.17</a>). Moreover, the pullback diagram of simplicial sets </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \emptyset \ar [r] \ar [d] &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_0 \ar [d]^{\iota _0} \\ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_1 \ar [r]^-{\iota _1} &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \]
</div>
<p> is also categorical pullback square (Corollary <a data-tag="033R" href="/tag/033R">4.5.3.28</a>), and therefore determines a pullback diagram in the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}$ (Example <a data-tag="03G7" href="/tag/03G7">7.6.3.4</a>). </p>
</article>
